  "description": "Tests macOS runs in post-integration full validation (the `darwin` test set). Linux runs the complete inventory once; macOS proves only what differs on the platform: the AArch64 LLVM backend (every llvm_* and macos_* test by prefix), the Apple-only registrations, threads/atomics/TLS/cthread runtime, debug info and lldb, install/bundle/package/link, ABI/layout/native C, and the default-backend runtime harnesses. Derived from the 2026-11-03 test-matrix review; a test not listed and not matching a prefix runs on Linux only. The compiler smoke always runs.",
